			<DIV CLASS="sectiontitle"><IMG SRC="http://demo.awayx.com/images/newsletter/icon_computer.gif" ALIGN="absmiddle" WIDTH="40" HEIGHT="40" ALT="" BORDER="0">Tips and tricks...</DIV>

			<BLOCKQUOTE>

			<UL>
				<LI><B>Shortcut</B><BR>To save time, in the login page, after typing in the username and password, press the enter key to log in.<BR><BR></LI>
				<LI><B>Refreshing</B><BR>To refresh a page, the easiest way is to right click on the page and select "refresh". This will only reload the section that you are working on, not the whole application.<BR><BR></LI>
				<LI><B>Using 2 Browsers</B><BR>
				While you are actively using the application; do not open another
				  browser window and navigate to the application login page. If you do, you
				  will be logged out of the application. This is a security feature and the
				  behavior is by design.<BR>
				<BR></LI>
				<LI><B>Extra Info</B><BR>
				Want more information on something like a <cfoutput>#application.returned_customer_setting.distributor_label_singular#</cfoutput>, product,
				  or program? Click using your right mouse button -- further details are
				  available. You can also try clicking on whatever you want more information
				  about. Sometimes we "hide" information to save space that we will show
				  if you click on a link.<BR>
				<BR></LI>
				<LI><B><CFOUTPUT>#application.returned_customer_setting.Trade_Label# #Application.PlannerLabel#</CFOUTPUT> to Work In Progress</B><BR>The <CFOUTPUT>#application.returned_customer_setting.Trade_Label# #Application.PlannerLabel#</CFOUTPUT> tool now has the ability to create a Work In Progress #Application.PlannerPrgLabel# on the fly. After you've created your Trade Plan, just click on the
					<B>[create WIP]</B> link at the bottom of the <CFOUTPUT>#application.returned_customer_setting.Trade_Label# #Application.PlannerLabel#</CFOUTPUT>, select a template and you will be brought to the Basic Information page in programs.
					Once you save your #Application.PlannerPrgLabel#, all the data from the <CFOUTPUT>#application.returned_customer_setting.Trade_Label# #Application.PlannerLabel#</CFOUTPUT> will be brought over into your #Application.PlannerPrgLabel#. This eliminates the extra step of taking data from the <CFOUTPUT>#application.returned_customer_setting.Trade_Label# #Application.PlannerLabel#</CFOUTPUT> and entering it
					into a #Application.PlannerPrgLabel#. </LI>
			</UL>
